  "question": {
    "text": "The velocity of a car travelling on a straight road is $3.6 \\mathrm{kmh}^{-1}$ at an instant of time. Now travelling with uniform acceleration for $10 \\mathrm{s}$, the velocity becomes exactly double. If the wheel radius of the car is $25 \\mathrm{cm}$, then which of the following is the closest to the number of revolutions that the wheel makes during this 10 s?"
  },
